2026-08-10T07:57:50.5197405Z         "retrieval_text": "Claim AKL-000067: When an ID Token is received by direct communication from the Token Endpoint, OpenID Connect clients MAY use TLS server validation to validate the issuer in place of checking that token's signature.\nSubject: AKC-000018\nPredicate: permits-direct-token-endpoint-tls-validation\nObject: {\"literal\":\"TLS issuer validation in place of signature checking for a directly received ID Token\"}\nClaim type: normalized-source-claim\nConfidence: high\nSemantic scope: concept-global\nConditions: [{\"concept_ids\":[],\"scope\":\"edge-local\",\"statement\":\"The ID Token is received by direct communication from the Token Endpoint.\"}]\nNormative: {\"applies_to\":\"OpenID Connect clients receiving an ID Token directly from the Token Endpoint.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"force\":\"may\"}\nSources: AKS-000019\nSource locators: [{\"locator\":\"OpenID Connect Core Section 3.1.3.7, item 6\",\"source_id\":\"AKS-000019\"}]",
